149:<p>Load it before even a small build, test, edit or measurement there, including long background runs you wait on, and when briefing agents for that work; <span class="cut">then</span> <span class="add">then, for a task that reads or changes the original tree (its Java and Scala, the library, the tests or the specification), or reviews such a change,</span> read references/revival-changes.md <span class="cut">whole before work.</span> <span class="add">whole.</span></p>
150:</div></div>
151:<div class="note"><p><strong>Why.</strong> The description told every worker to read the revival part whole, which no longer agreed with the rule of change 2. It now asks it only of a task that reads, changes or reviews the original tree, in the same words as &ldquo;The parts&rdquo;, since the first wording, &ldquo;Fortress code&rdquo;, could mean Fortress source or the Java and Scala.</p></div>
