167:<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">New text; underlined, the words that changed; struck through, the words that went</span>
168:<p class="where-in">compiler.md, &ldquo;The compiler's prelude, until the switch-over&rdquo;, line 34</p>
169:<p>Do not add a declaration to the three prelude files: they are deleted at the switch-over. Their tests stay. <span class="add">If a helper of <code>nativeHelpers/</code> that the one library binds is wrong, fix the helper's Java, even where the prelude binds it too. Do not edit the prelude's text: its binding then gives the fixed result. If a compiled test pinned the old result, change the test with the helper, as for any fixed defect.</span></p>
170:</div></div>
171:<div class="note"><p><strong>Why.</strong> The part did not say what to do with a wrong helper that both the one library and the prelude bind. The text now says to fix the helper's Java and leave the prelude's text alone, so that the prelude's result changes with the helper, as its printing of unsigned numbers did in climb batch 25 [P-38, F-313].</p></div>
