187:<p><span class="add">A trait or object that extends a generic trait compiles with <code>Any</code> as the static argument. With <code>Bottom</code>, <code>Self</code> or an abbreviated type there, the code generator refuses the declaration. An abbreviated type is a short form that the specification gives for a type, such as <code>RR64[3]</code> for an array type. With a tuple that holds <code>Any</code> there, the code generator crashes (ledger row 889).</span></p>
